WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.790
Choose a safe resting position, lying down or well supported.

2
00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:16.800
Adjust blankets, clothing, or posture if you are physically too warm, cold, numb, or uncomfortable.

3
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:30.650
This practice is about noticing ordinary sensation, not enduring discomfort or creating a particular temperature.

4
00:00:33.881 --> 00:00:37.796
Begin with the places where the body meets support.

5
00:00:39.496 --> 00:00:44.626
Feel the broad fact of contact before searching for detail.

6
00:00:46.326 --> 00:00:54.421
The surface may feel firm, soft, cool, warm, or difficult to describe.

7
00:00:59.806 --> 00:01:01.806
Notice where weight is clearest.

8
00:01:03.506 --> 00:01:11.231
Perhaps the head, shoulders, back, pelvis, legs, or heels.

9
00:01:12.931 --> 00:01:18.031
Let one region be heavy enough to be received by the surface.

10
00:01:19.731 --> 00:01:23.776
You do not need to make it heavier.

11
00:01:30.507 --> 00:01:32.347
Bring attention to the hands.

12
00:01:34.047 --> 00:01:37.847
One hand may feel warmer than the other.

13
00:01:39.547 --> 00:01:47.807
The palms may hold warmth while the backs feel cool, or there may be no clear difference.

14
00:01:49.507 --> 00:01:51.667
Stay with what is actually present.

15
00:01:58.398 --> 00:02:03.048
Notice the temperature of air or fabric at the fingers.

16
00:02:04.748 --> 00:02:09.308
Then notice the deeper sense of the hands' weight.

17
00:02:11.008 --> 00:02:17.548
Temperature and weight can be known together without needing to choose between them.

18
00:02:24.279 --> 00:02:25.759
Move attention to the feet.

19
00:02:27.459 --> 00:02:32.554
Feel socks, bedding, floor, or air.

20
00:02:34.254 --> 00:02:41.864
Perhaps there is warmth, coolness, tingling, pressure, or very little.

21
00:02:43.564 --> 00:02:50.784
If sensation is unclear, notice the known shape and position of the feet instead.

22
00:02:57.515 --> 00:02:59.755
Let both legs enter awareness.

23
00:03:01.455 --> 00:03:03.535
Sense their length and broad weight.

24
00:03:05.235 --> 00:03:10.910
One leg may seem heavier, lighter, warmer, or cooler.

25
00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:16.325
The two sides do not need to match.

26
00:03:24.402 --> 00:03:31.022
Notice where the legs are supported and where there is space beneath them.

27
00:03:32.722 --> 00:03:34.842
Let the support carry what it can.

28
00:03:36.542 --> 00:03:46.988
If the body asks for a small adjustment, make it and feel how the map of pressure changes.

29
00:03:53.719 --> 00:03:57.929
Bring attention to the pelvis and lower back.

30
00:03:59.629 --> 00:04:09.814
This central region may feel dense, light, broad, warm, cool, comfortable, or uncomfortable.

31
00:04:11.514 --> 00:04:17.734
Use simple words if words help, then return to direct sensation.

32
00:04:25.811 --> 00:04:30.471
Feel the belly and ribs moving with an ordinary breath.

33
00:04:32.171 --> 00:04:37.061
The inhale may bring a slight lift or expansion.

34
00:04:38.761 --> 00:04:46.861
The exhale may bring a sense of settling, or no change at all.

35
00:04:48.561 --> 00:04:50.961
Do not push the body toward heaviness.

36
00:04:59.038 --> 00:05:01.558
Notice the chest and upper back.

37
00:05:03.258 --> 00:05:09.348
Temperature may vary where clothing, air, or support touches the skin.

38
00:05:11.048 --> 00:05:15.288
Weight may be clearer at the back than the front.

39
00:05:16.988 --> 00:05:21.778
Let the whole torso be one changing field.

40
00:05:29.856 --> 00:05:32.816
Bring attention to the shoulders and arms.

41
00:05:34.516 --> 00:05:42.826
Feel the weight of the upper arms, elbows, forearms, and hands as one continuous path.

42
00:05:44.526 --> 00:05:50.816
Imagine no change; simply recognize what the surface is already holding.

43
00:05:58.893 --> 00:06:00.213
Notice the face.

44
00:06:01.913 --> 00:06:08.453
Air may feel cool near the nose and warmth may gather around the eyes or cheeks.

45
00:06:10.153 --> 00:06:11.753
There may be no contrast.

46
00:06:13.453 --> 00:06:19.953
Include the weight of the head and the place where it is supported.

47
00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:31.230
Now widen attention from head to feet.

48
00:06:32.930 --> 00:06:40.910
Warm areas, cool areas, heavy areas, light or almost absent areas.

49
00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:43.970
None is more correct.

50
00:06:45.670 --> 00:06:48.270
Sensation can shift while you listen.

51
00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:00.720
See whether warmth has an edge.

52
00:07:02.420 --> 00:07:06.875
Does it stop clearly or fade into another temperature?

53
00:07:08.575 --> 00:07:15.155
See whether weight has an edge, or spreads into the support beneath you.

54
00:07:16.855 --> 00:07:19.535
There is no need to answer precisely.

55
00:07:28.958 --> 00:07:34.168
Notice a sound in the room while continuing to feel the body.

56
00:07:35.868 --> 00:07:43.528
Sound has no weight, yet it can share the same moment with pressure, temperature, and breath.

57
00:07:51.606 --> 00:08:02.361
Let attention rest on the single clearest sensation, whether warm, cool, heavy, light, or neutral.

58
00:08:04.061 --> 00:08:06.421
Stay for three natural breaths.

59
00:08:08.121 --> 00:08:13.681
If the sensation changes, follow the change without trying to keep it.

60
00:08:24.450 --> 00:08:28.780
Return to the whole body's contact with support.

61
00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:32.760
Gravity continues without instruction.

62
00:08:34.460 --> 00:08:37.181
The surface continues to respond.

63
00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:42.970
For a few moments, let being carried be enough.

64
00:08:55.086 --> 00:08:57.486
Begin to recognize the room more fully.

65
00:08:59.186 --> 00:09:06.801
Notice air on the skin, light through the eyes or eyelids, and sounds near and far.

66
00:09:08.501 --> 00:09:13.061
Feel the body as both weighted and able to move.

67
00:09:18.446 --> 00:09:23.481
Invite a small movement into fingers and toes.

68
00:09:25.181 --> 00:09:31.606
If you are getting up, change position slowly and pause before standing.

69
00:09:33.306 --> 00:09:40.406
If you are continuing to rest, let the movement fade.

70
00:09:44.445 --> 00:09:50.390
Warmth, coolness, weight, and lightness did not need to be produced.

71
00:09:52.090 --> 00:10:00.000
You practiced noticing how the body is here, and how support meets it now.
